  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 255 PM EDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\n- Chance for thunderstorms Wednesday, maybe some severe weather\n\nCold front on track for Wednesday with some light showers still\npossible early in the morning. Main time frame for any severe\nweather still looks to be noonish and after with all weather\nclearing the area by 8pm. Morning showers should be pretty\nscattered and are likely to inhibit afternoon storm potential for\na good deal of the area - especially north of I-96 and west of\nUS-131. Some warm/moist air will build in ahead of the front into\nsouthern lower Michigan...where best potential for destabilization\nwill occur mid-afternoon into the early evening. This leaves the\nbest potential for severe weather near I-94 and east of\nUS-131...probably closer to US-127 and east.",
